# Browser harness: dependencies and the scratch copy of the pinned specs are artifacts.
node_modules/
.pinned-run/
test-results/
generation-probe-report.json

# PER-RUN LEGS ARE NOT COMMITTED. A leg is the evidence for ONE run, not an expectation: the committed
# artifact is the *-comparison.json, which records the DIFFERENCES and the checks. A committed leg would
# invite someone to treat a known divergence as the expected value.
#
# PATTERNS, NOT ONE RUN'S NAMES. The first version of this file listed the exact names a single run
# happened to use (`stream-gotavern.json`, `cancel-pinned.json`, ...). Later runs name their legs after
# the SOURCE (`stream-or-gotavern.json` for openrouter, `gen-or-pinned.json`), write their data-domain
# captures as `dd2-g1.json`, and their extension legs as `ext-th-A6-leg.json` -- none of which matched,
# so every re-record would leave 100-250 KB of untracked debris beside the gated artifact, where a
# reader can mistake one for a gate input. tests/browser/catalog.test.mjs asserts that the patterns
# below cover every leg name the committed artifacts actually record AND that none of them matches a
# committed `*-comparison.json`, so a new naming scheme fails the test instead of escaping the list.
#
# No pattern below can match a `*-comparison.json`: each is anchored on the `-` that separates a prefix
# from a leg suffix (gen-, stream-, cancel-, nonstream-, startup-<leg>-<n>, dd<n>-<leg>).

# Generation legs: gen-a.json, gen-p1.json, gen-or-gotavern.json, gen-groq-pinned.json ...
gen-*.json
# Streaming, cancellation and non-stream controls: stream-gotavern.json, stream-or-pinned.json,
# cancel-mistral-gotavern.json, nonstream-openai-pinned.json ...
stream-*.json
cancel-*.json
nonstream-*.json
# THE SAME SURFACES WITH A SOURCE PREFIX IN FRONT. The committed artifacts record legs named
# `mis-stream-a.json` / `mis-cancel-p.json` (mistral) and `stream-cl-gotavern.json` (claude), so the
# surface is not always the first token. Without these three, a mistral re-record leaves six files beside
# the gated artifact -- which is exactly what the old exact-name list did.
*-stream-*.json
*-cancel-*.json
*-nonstream-*.json
# Startup captures: startup-gotavern-1.json, startup-pinned-2.json ...
startup-gotavern-*.json
startup-pinned-*.json
# Data-domain captures: the original `data-domain-*` names and the `dd2-*` names a later run used.
data-domain-gotavern-*.json
data-domain-pinned-*.json
dd*-*.json
# Extension E2E legs: extension-tavern-helper-gotavern.json, and the `ext-th-A6-leg.json` shape a later
# run used. `*-leg.json` is the general form, so a new prefix (a second extension) is covered too.
extension-*-gotavern.json
extension-*-pinned.json
*-leg.json
# COMPLEX-PRESET LEGS: preset-keep-gotavern.json, preset-keep-pinned.json, preset-drop-gotavern.json,
# preset-drop-pinned.json. The committed artefact is `preset-complex-comparison.json`, which matches
# NEITHER pattern: the boundary variant is anchored on the `-`, so a committed `preset-complex-*` name can
# never be swallowed by the ignore list (tests/browser/catalog.test.mjs asserts both directions).
preset-keep-*.json
preset-drop-*.json
